@startuml
' WCTO / B4SC FHIR resource data model - corrected DRAFT
' SOURCE LOCATION: <repo>/diagrams/fhir-data-model.puml
' RENDER OUTPUT: <repo>/input/images/wcto-fhir-data-model.svg
' Replaces the earlier conceptual diagram; NOT a validated profile specification.
' Confirm all links and cardinalities against the repository FSH and FHIR R4B.
left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam class { BorderColor #6B8299; ArrowColor #51758F }
hide empty methods
hide circle

package "National / external authoritative sources" #E9F3FC {
  class "NHI\nidentity" as NHI #D8ECFC
  class "NES\nenrolment" as NES #D8ECFC
  class "HPI\nworkforce and organisation" as HPI #D8ECFC
  class "AIR\nimmunisation" as AIR #D8ECFC
  class "PMS / EMR\nexisting clinical information" as PMS #D8ECFC
}

package "People and provider context" #EAF8F6 {
  class "Patient\n(NZ Base where applicable)" as Patient #D9F0FA {
    identifier (NHI)
    name / birthDate
  }
  class "RelatedPerson" as RelatedPerson #E4E0FF {
    patient
    relationship
  }
  class "Practitioner" as Practitioner #D9F0FA {
    identifier (HPI where available)
  }
  class "PractitionerRole" as PractitionerRole #D9F0FA {
    practitioner
    organization
    code
  }
  class "Organization" as Organization #D9F0FA {
    identifier (HPI where applicable)
  }
  class "CareTeam" as CareTeam #E4E0FF {
    subject
    participant
  }
}

package "WCTO / B4SC workflow" #FFF3E5 {
  class "B4SC PlanDefinition\n(workflow template)" as PlanDefinition #FCE5CA {
    url / version
    action
  }
  class "WCTO B4SC CarePlan\n(profile)" as CarePlan #FBD9AF {
    subject
    status
    intent
    category
    careTeam
  }
  class "WCTO B4SC Task\n(profile)" as Task #E9DFFF {
    basedOn
    for
    status
    businessStatus
    owner
    focus / output (where defined)
  }
  class "ServiceRequest\n(referral, if adopted)" as ServiceRequest #DDF4EB {
    subject
    reasonCode / reasonReference
    status
  }
  class "Consent\n(if adopted as resource)" as Consent #DDF4EB {
    patient
    performer
    status
  }
}

package "Forms, provenance and clinical data" #F0F8FF {
  class "Questionnaire\n(per form definition)" as Questionnaire #D8ECFC {
    url / version
    item.linkId
  }
  class "QuestionnaireResponse\n(per captured contribution)" as QR #D8ECFC {
    questionnaire (canonical)
    subject
    author / source
    authored
    status
    item / answer
    meta.versionId (server-managed)
  }
  class "Provenance\n(review / amendment events)" as Provenance #E4E0FF {
    target
    recorded
    agent
    activity
  }
  class "Observation\n(selected extracted findings)" as Observation #DDF4EB
  class "Condition\n(if clinically reconciled)" as Condition #DDF4EB
  class "AllergyIntolerance\n(if clinically reconciled)" as Allergy #DDF4EB
  class "MedicationStatement\n(if clinically reconciled)" as Medication #DDF4EB
  class "Immunization\n(AIR sourced)" as Immunization #DDF4EB
  class "DocumentReference\n(summary / PDF where adopted)" as DocRef #DDF4EB
  class "Composition\n(structured document where adopted)" as Composition #DDF4EB
}

RelatedPerson --> Patient : patient
PractitionerRole --> Practitioner : practitioner
PractitionerRole --> Organization : organization
CareTeam --> Patient : subject
CareTeam ..> PractitionerRole : participant (as supported)
CarePlan --> Patient : subject
CarePlan ..> CareTeam : careTeam
Task --> CarePlan : basedOn (agreed design)
Task --> Patient : for
Task ..> PractitionerRole : owner (where used)
Task ..> QR : focus / output\n(implementation mapping TBD)
PlanDefinition ..> Task : workflow orchestration\ncreates tasks (application logic)
PlanDefinition ..> CarePlan : applied by orchestration\n(not a direct reference)
QR --> Questionnaire : questionnaire (canonical)
QR --> Patient : subject
QR ..> RelatedPerson : author / source\n(where appropriate)
QR ..> Practitioner : author / source\n(where appropriate)
Provenance --> QR : target
Provenance ..> Practitioner : agent (example)
Provenance ..> RelatedPerson : agent (example)
QR ..> Observation : extraction, only if mapped
QR ..> Condition : reconciliation, if required
QR ..> Allergy : reconciliation, if required
QR ..> Medication : reconciliation, if required
ServiceRequest --> Patient : subject
Task ..> ServiceRequest : focus / basedOn as designed
Consent --> Patient : patient
DocRef --> Patient : subject
Composition --> Patient : subject
NHI ..> Patient : authoritative identity
NES ..> Patient : enrolment lookup (not ownership)
HPI ..> PractitionerRole : authoritative role context
HPI ..> Organization : authoritative organisation
AIR ..> Immunization : authoritative source
PMS ..> Condition : existing clinical context\nif authorised

note bottom of Task
  Business workflow (not native Task.status codes):
  Whanau forms, consent and vision/hearing may
  progress concurrently, in any order.
  Nurse evaluation is the final clinical gate.
  Task.status uses valid FHIR codes; finer
  stages use businessStatus / application rules.
end note
note bottom of QR
  QuestionnaireResponse.status reflects response state,
  NOT overall B4SC completion or nurse sign-off.
  Preserve original submissions; use Provenance
  and server version history where supported.
  Do not invent QuestionnaireResponse.version.
end note
note bottom of PlanDefinition
  The diagram is a candidate architecture.
  No unsupported fixed cardinalities are asserted.
  Confirm all FSH constraints and data mapping
  before publishing as normative.
end note

legend bottom
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#D8ECFC> | Identity / form definition and response |
|<#FBD9AF> | WCTO workflow resource |
|<#E9DFFF> | Supporting workflow / provenance / participant |
|<#DDF4EB> | Clinical resource / output (when adopted) |
|<#D8ECFC> | National source shown in external package |
Solid arrow: candidate FHIR reference where supported
Dotted arrow: conditional / conceptual mapping or orchestration
endlegend
@enduml
